Ultimately, you didn't really need either one of them, did you?

00:37:03.199 --> 00:37:05.199
I don't know about that.

00:37:05.199 --> 00:37:11.199
I mean, I'm more partial to sporks myself, but a girl can never have too many spoons.

00:37:11.199 --> 00:37:13.199
Yeah, well, I never should have around.

00:37:13.199 --> 00:37:17.199
I popped up that Pandora's box to begin with and second guess myself or us.

00:37:17.199 --> 00:37:19.199
From now on, I won't.

00:37:19.199 --> 00:37:23.199
Maybe we should just say that next time you won't take advice about relationships from Clark Kent.

00:37:23.199 --> 00:37:32.039
You know, speaking of Clark, for future reference, and, you know,

00:37:32.039 --> 00:37:34.039
strictly for environmental purposes,

00:37:34.039 --> 00:37:37.039
the next time you want to take a shower with someone, Chloe, you can just ask me.

00:37:37.039 --> 00:37:40.039
I can't remember blacking out, and I wish I could forget waking up.

00:37:40.039 --> 00:37:43.039
Really? Well, it couldn't have been that bad, right?

00:37:43.039 --> 00:37:45.039
Wasn't there a time when you would have given just about anything

00:37:45.039 --> 00:37:46.039
to stare at that farmer's tan and all its glory.

00:37:46.039 --> 00:37:47.039
and all it's glory, I'm guessing.

00:37:47.039 --> 00:37:52.039
That was a long time ago, like, in a smallville far, far away.

00:37:52.039 --> 00:37:56.800
I mean, okay, yeah, I did love Clark.

00:37:56.800 --> 00:37:58.800
A lot.

00:37:58.800 --> 00:38:03.800
And I waited for years for him to see that, to see me.

00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:06.800
But even with his X-ray vision, he never did.

00:38:06.800 --> 00:38:10.800
I think more than that, I just wanted someone who would get me.

00:38:10.800 --> 00:38:17.780
And as good a friend as Clark is, he's never going to be that person,

00:38:17.780 --> 00:38:19.780
which is fine.

00:38:19.780 --> 00:38:23.369
I mean, those wounds.

00:38:23.369 --> 00:38:25.369
healed over a thousand super saves ago.

